# E2E Theme Testing Technical Insights

## Applies To
- **File Pattern**: `**/e2e/**/*.spec.ts`, `**/e2e/**/*.test.ts`
- **When Working On**: Playwright e2e tests, theme-related functionality, UI component testing
- **Related Files**: Theme providers, theme toggles, settings pages

## Overview
Technical insights and patterns for testing theme switching functionality in Playwright e2e tests, based on lessons learned from fixing failing theme tests.

## Key Technical Issues & Solutions

### 1. Theme Provider Behavior
- **App Default**: Uses `defaultTheme="system"` in [AppLayout](mdc:packages/app-shell/src/app-layout.tsx)
- **DOM Application**: Theme classes (`light`/`dark`) are applied to `document.documentElement` (html element)
- **System Theme**: When theme is `system`, it applies either `light` or `dark` class based on `prefers-color-scheme`
- **State vs DOM**: Theme state (`system`) differs from applied DOM class (`light` or `dark`)

### 2. Theme Toggle Logic Limitations
- **Toggle Implementation**: [ThemeToggle](mdc:packages/ui/src/theme-toggle.tsx) uses `theme === 'light' ? 'dark' : 'light'`
- **System Theme Issue**: When current theme is `system`, toggle sets to `light` (not ideal UX)
- **Test Implication**: Tests must account for this behavior or set explicit theme states

### 3. Common Test Failures & Fixes

#### Text Selector Ambiguity
```typescript
// ❌ Problematic - matches multiple elements
await expect(page.getByText('Theme')).toBeVisible();

// ✅ Fixed - exact match only
await expect(page.getByText('Theme', { exact: true })).toBeVisible();
```

#### Theme State Initialization
```typescript
// ❌ Problematic - assumes initial state
const htmlElement = page.locator('html');
await expect(htmlElement).not.toHaveClass(/dark/); // May fail if system is dark

// ✅ Fixed - set known state first
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Settings', exact: true }).click();
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Light' }).click();
await page.waitForTimeout(100);
// Now test from known state
```

#### DOM Update Timing
```typescript
// ❌ Problematic - immediate assertion
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Dark' }).click();
await expect(htmlElement).toHaveClass(/dark/); // May fail due to timing

// ✅ Fixed - wait for DOM update
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Dark' }).click();
await page.waitForTimeout(100);
await expect(htmlElement).toHaveClass(/dark/);
```

#### Page Reload Navigation
```typescript
// ❌ Problematic - assumes page stays on same route
await page.reload();
await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Settings' })).toBeVisible();

// ✅ Fixed - account for actual navigation behavior
await page.reload();
await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Context Explorer' })).toBeVisible();
```

## Test Patterns

### Reliable Theme Testing Pattern
```typescript
test('theme functionality', async ({ page }) => {
  // 1. Navigate to settings
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Settings', exact: true }).click();
  
  // 2. Set explicit theme state
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Light' }).click();
  await page.waitForTimeout(100);
  
  // 3. Test theme changes with timing
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Dark' }).click();
  await page.waitForTimeout(100);
  
  // 4. Assert DOM state
  const htmlElement = page.locator('html');
  await expect(htmlElement).toHaveClass(/dark/);
  
  // 5. Test persistence across navigation
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Context Explorer' }).click();
  await expect(htmlElement).toHaveClass(/dark/);
});
```

### Theme Toggle Testing
- Always set explicit theme state before testing toggle
- Account for system theme behavior in toggle logic
- Use timing delays for DOM updates
- Test both settings buttons and navigation toggle

